    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Burning on passing urine for two days. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Higuchi called this morning and was seen the same day. For two days she has had burning when she passes urine, needing to go often and urgently, and a dull ache low in her abdomen. She has no fever, chills, back or flank pain, nausea or vomiting, and no vaginal discharge or itching. She has never had a urinary infection before. She has not been sexually active and is not pregnant. She admits she has been drinking little while writing for long stretches at her desk on hot days. She is in the fourteenth week of tuberculosis treatment, in the continuation phase on isoniazid and rifampin, and has taken every dose on video with the public health center; her urine is orange from rifampin, as expected. Her cough has gone and she is gaining weight. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Burning, frequency, urgency and lower abdominal ache</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; no fever</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Continuation phase of tuberculosis treatment on isoniazid and rifampin; drinking little</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No flank pain, fever, vomiting or vaginal discharge</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

